== 9.9 Chapter 9 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Nitrogen is needed by a crop mainly for],
  [seed germination],
  [root growth],
  [fruit colour],
  [leaves and vegetative growth]
)

#mcq(2, [Phosphorus is most important for],
  [disease resistance],
  [leaf colour],
  [water uptake only],
  [root growth, flowering and fruiting]
)

#mcq(3, [Potassium improves mainly],
  [root depth],
  [disease resistance and fruit quality],
  [leaf size],
  [germination]
)

#mcq(4, [A fertiliser labelled NPK 20:10:10 contains],
  [20 % nitrogen, 10 % phosphorus, 10 % potassium],
  [20 % phosphorus, 10 % potassium],
  [equal amounts of all three],
  [20 % potassium, 10 % nitrogen, 10 % phosphorus]
)

#mcq(5, [The main advantage of manure over artificial fertiliser is that manure],
  [is easier to transport],
  [is more concentrated],
  [acts faster],
  [improves soil structure and adds humus]
)

#mcq(6, [A disadvantage of artificial fertiliser is that it],
  [acts too slowly],
  [can be leached and pollute water],
  [improves structure],
  [adds humus]
)

#mcq(7, [Acid soil is corrected by adding],
  [calcium carbonate (lime)],
  [sodium chloride],
  [ammonium sulphate],
  [urea]
)

#mcq(8, [Monoculture is],
  [growing a legume after a cereal],
  [growing two crops together],
  [growing the same crop on the same land every year],
  [leaving the land fallow]
)

#mcq(9, [Crop rotation helps to control pests because],
  [it adds pesticide],
  [it changes the climate],
  [it kills the pests chemically],
  [the pest's host is absent in some years]
)

#mcq(10, [A legume is included in a rotation because it],
  [resists all pests],
  [needs no water],
  [adds nitrogen through *Rhizobium*],
  [is a heavy feeder]
)

#mcq(11, [Mixed cropping has the advantage of],
  [spreading the risk of crop failure],
  [easier harvesting],
  [higher single-crop yield],
  [easier mechanisation]
)

#mcq(12, [A fallow period allows the soil to],
  [dry out completely],
  [regain fertility and structure],
  [become saline],
  [lose all humus]
)

#mcq(13, [Plant breeding by crossing two varieties is called],
  [selection],
  [hybridisation],
  [mutation breeding],
  [genetic engineering]
)

#mcq(14, [A crop variety bred for short maturity is useful because it],
  [can be harvested before the dry season ends],
  [resists no pests],
  [yields less],
  [needs more water]
)

#mcq(15, [The aim of crop improvement is *not* to],
  [improve nutritional quality],
  [increase yield],
  [improve disease resistance],
  [increase susceptibility to pests]
)

#mcq(16, [Pests of stored grain include],
  [mosses],
  [lichens],
  [weevils],
  [cattle]
)

#mcq(17, [A biological method of pest control is],
  [releasing a natural predator],
  [using resistant varieties],
  [rotating crops],
  [spraying insecticide]
)

#mcq(18, [The repeated use of one pesticide leads to],
  [resistance in the pest population],
  [fewer pests for ever],
  [better control each year],
  [increased soil humus]
)

#mcq(19, [Pesticides may cause a pest resurgence because they],
  [increase the pest's food],
  [kill the pest's natural enemies],
  [make the crop tastier],
  [raise the temperature]
)

#mcq(20, [Ruminants can digest cellulose because of],
  [enzymes in the saliva],
  [strong stomach acid],
  [a large caecum],
  [micro-organisms in the rumen]
)

#mcq(21, [The true stomach of a ruminant is the],
  [abomasum],
  [rumen],
  [omasum],
  [reticulum]
)

#mcq(22, [Which animal is a non-ruminant?],
  [Goat],
  [Pig],
  [Sheep],
  [Cow]
)

#mcq(23, [Cud chewing is associated with the],
  [abomasum],
  [liver],
  [rumen and reticulum],
  [small intestine]
)

#mcq(24, [A disease of cattle spread by the tsetse fly is],
  [foot and mouth disease],
  [trypanosomiasis],
  [Newcastle disease],
  [anthrax]
)

#mcq(25, [Newcastle disease affects],
  [fish],
  [cattle],
  [poultry],
  [goats]
)

#mcq(26, [Vaccination of livestock is a form of],
  [treatment after infection],
  [culling],
  [prevention before exposure],
  [quarantine]
)

#mcq(27, [Food is preserved by salting because salt],
  [adds nutrients],
  [draws water out of microbial cells],
  [increases acidity],
  [kills all bacteria]
)

#mcq(28, [Refrigeration preserves food by],
  [killing micro-organisms],
  [removing water],
  [slowing their growth and enzyme action],
  [adding acid]
)

#mcq(29, [Aflatoxin is produced by],
  [bacteria in the soil],
  [*Aspergillus* moulds on damp grain],
  [weevils in the store],
  [rats in the field]
)

#mcq(30, [Canning preserves food because],
  [the food is dried first],
  [salt is added],
  [the food is frozen],
  [heat sterilises the food and the sealed can excludes air]
)

